(6436795, 953771, 63218, '<td valign="top">Nice light modeling the FG flower. Can''t help but wonder why you didn''t clean up the specks on the BG but at least I got a freshly-polished screen out of it "D</td>', 'Nice light modeling the FG flower. Can''t help but wonder why you didn''t clean up the specks on the BG but at least I got a freshly-polished screen out of it "D', '2011-06-07 09:56:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6436799, 953752, 12611, '<td valign="top">The feel of this shot is great- the trees and the engine with the dirt beside them. There is a soft yellowness over the whole shot that also masks the bright daylight- but the composition is a bit lacking- and this is a free study- with need for your "A" game- this is a B+</td>', 'The feel of this shot is great- the trees and the engine with the dirt beside them. There is a soft yellowness over the whole shot that also masks the bright daylight- but the composition is a bit lacking- and this is a free study- with need for your "A" game- this is a B+', '2011-06-07 10:02:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(6436801, 952947, 12611, '<td valign="top">What terrific clarity; I think the above blur is a bit too dark.</td>', 'What terrific clarity; I think the above blur is a bit too dark.', '2011-06-07 10:05:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(6436802, 954408, 12611, '<td valign="top">I really dig this one- stark post- impressionist but still austere, wonderful lighting; perfect placement of the umbrellas. great wood texture- a fine entry!</td>', 'I really dig this one- stark post- impressionist but still austere, wonderful lighting; perfect placement of the umbrellas. great wood texture- a fine entry!', '2011-06-07 10:08:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6436805, 953622, 12611, '<td valign="top">I like I a whole lot- theres a nice primitive religious renaissance painting feel here- and that works even in bright sunlight, almost panoramic in effect. perhaps this would work better and be "stunning" or have that much needed "wow factor" if you took the shot really wide angle with the camera on the ground and the lens at a 45 degree angle with the ground- that would avoid the distractingly strong presence of the spires behind the facade.</td>', 'I like I a whole lot- theres a nice primitive religious renaissance painting feel here- and that works even in bright sunlight, almost panoramic in effect. perhaps this would work better and be "stunning" or have that much needed "wow factor" if you took the shot really wide angle with the camera on the ground and the lens at a 45 degree angle with the ground- that would avoid the distractingly strong presence of the spires behind the facade.', '2011-06-07 10:12:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(6436806, 954687, 12611, '<td valign="top">I like the aspect ratio and the border. the sky lends the apparent wrath. I like a pretty shot with a touch of wrath- and you nailed that, the relevance of Steinbeck being important or not.</td>', 'I like the aspect ratio and the border. the sky lends the apparent wrath. I like a pretty shot with a touch of wrath- and you nailed that, the relevance of Steinbeck being important or not.', '2011-06-07 10:13:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(6436813, 952600, 12611, '<td valign="top">Nice title. I just read somewhere that "fairies" or "faerie" and later interpretations, such as Tolkien''s "elves" are really the same thing. Not the little fairies the size of butterflies- the tinkerbells, but fairies like the green night in "Sir Gawain and the Green knight." big mean faerie- elves.<br/> <br/>sorry for the arcane discussion- nice albino deer in there.perfect placement/</td>', 'Nice title. I just read somewhere that "fairies" or "faerie" and later interpretations, such as Tolkien''s "elves" are really the same thing. Not the little fairies the size of butterflies- the tinkerbells, but fairies like the green night in "Sir Gawain and the Green knight." big mean faerie- elves. sorry for the arcane discussion- nice albino deer in there.perfect placement/', '2011-06-07 10:18:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(6436815, 952684, 12611, '<td valign="top">I like it- love the vague title- is he a reluctant groom? a washed up lounge singer? A best man in love with the bride? we the viewer with have to wait until it is our "turn to tell"<br/>great lighting and contrast, especially on his face. great shot.</td>', 'I like it- love the vague title- is he a reluctant groom? a washed up lounge singer? A best man in love with the bride? we the viewer with have to wait until it is our "turn to tell"great lighting and contrast, especially on his face. great shot.', '2011-06-07 10:20:49.000000', NULL, 1),
