(6438557, 954698, 50695, '<td valign="top">oh wait, this picture has something to do with our relationship...</td>', 'oh wait, this picture has something to do with our relationship...', '2011-06-08 13:21:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(6438559, 954543, 112972, '<td valign="top">Only you can finish this high in a Free Study with a candid street shot like this, congrats!</td>', 'Only you can finish this high in a Free Study with a candid street shot like this, congrats!', '2011-06-08 13:26:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(6438560, 950820, 66384, '<td valign="top">You''re developing a body of work with these dramatic portraits of women with dogs. Very nice! I like the way you have the women gazing elsewhere while the dogs stare straight at the camera. Love the set, the light, and the tone in this one.</td>', 'You''re developing a body of work with these dramatic portraits of women with dogs. Very nice! I like the way you have the women gazing elsewhere while the dogs stare straight at the camera. Love the set, the light, and the tone in this one.', '2011-06-08 13:26:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(6438565, 953828, 50641, '<td valign="top">Not exactly a shabby score for FS...  Amazing capture.  You have great contrast, depth and sharpness.  However this all makes birdy''s head blend in with his wing. Maybe a little softening on the far wing would help - a post hoc dof adjustment of sorts.  As others mentioned, the light blue-gray background might have been an issue.  Perhaps opting for all sepia and then torquing up the golds and whites might have warmed things up a little, although it would make it less clinically accurate.</td>', 'Not exactly a shabby score for FS...  Amazing capture.  You have great contrast, depth and sharpness.  However this all makes birdy''s head blend in with his wing. Maybe a little softening on the far wing would help - a post hoc dof adjustment of sorts.  As others mentioned, the light blue-gray background might have been an issue.  Perhaps opting for all sepia and then torquing up the golds and whites might have warmed things up a little, although it would make it less clinically accurate.', '2011-06-08 13:28:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(6438567, 953704, 112972, '<td valign="top">Great makeup and beautiful model.  I know you said that this is an unedited photo, but I bet with a tiny bit more contrast, this would have won a ribbon.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-06-08 12:30:24.</i></td>', 'Great makeup and beautiful model.  I know you said that this is an unedited photo, but I bet with a tiny bit more contrast, this would have won a ribbon.', '2011-06-08 13:30:06.000000', '2011-06-08 13:30:24.000000', 0),
(6438583, 954298, 100831, '<td valign="top">This was one of my highest scores. I love the palette and the little blur. Great picture.</td>', 'This was one of my highest scores. I love the palette and the little blur. Great picture.', '2011-06-08 13:37:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(6438588, 953117, 103142, '<td valign="top">I think I already told you this, but I''ll repeat it anyway... :D<br/> <br/>The first time I saw it, I thought it was glorious and would have given it an 8. Now, for some reason, it just doesn''t seem to glow as much as when I first saw it. It almost makes me curious whether it''s daytime or nighttime viewing differences.</td>', 'I think I already told you this, but I''ll repeat it anyway... :D The first time I saw it, I thought it was glorious and would have given it an 8. Now, for some reason, it just doesn''t seem to glow as much as when I first saw it. It almost makes me curious whether it''s daytime or nighttime viewing differences.', '2011-06-08 13:42:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(6438589, 951622, 100831, '<td valign="top">such good seeing.</td>', 'such good seeing.', '2011-06-08 13:43:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(6438590, 954664, 35804, '<td valign="top">I was your lonely "10" vote. What I enjoyed most about this was the atmosphere/mood. The softness of the background coupled with the almost unaware-of-the-camera expression just really clicked for me. It''s like a shot that you would take between the fully camera aware/posed shots...she looks relaxed, and that''s how you want a model to look. ( Many of my personal favorite portraits are the "in betweens" as I like to call them.) I just found it refreshing, different...not a typical forced sort of fashion shot. Keep doing what you''re doing.</td>', 'I was your lonely "10" vote. What I enjoyed most about this was the atmosphere/mood. The softness of the background coupled with the almost unaware-of-the-camera expression just really clicked for me. It''s like a shot that you would take between the fully camera aware/posed shots...she looks relaxed, and that''s how you want a model to look. ( Many of my personal favorite portraits are the "in betweens" as I like to call them.) I just found it refreshing, different...not a typical forced sort of fashion shot. Keep doing what you''re doing.', '2011-06-08 13:44:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(6438593, 954442, 100831, '<td valign="top">.... looks like you had a great time, learned something, and got a wonderful entry out of it all!</td>', '.... looks like you had a great time, learned something, and got a wonderful entry out of it all!', '2011-06-08 13:46:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(6438610, 951393, 100831, '<td valign="top">that it is. What a wonderful capture and a great finish for you!!</td>', 'that it is. What a wonderful capture and a great finish for you!!', '2011-06-08 13:55:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(6438611, 951152, 100831, '<td valign="top">ohhhhh pretty looooong exposure!! Love it!</td>', 'ohhhhh pretty looooong exposure!! Love it!', '2011-06-08 13:57:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(6438618, 954238, 81042, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LydiaToo:</b></div><hr/><i> Nope.... I don''t understand similar entry either... She''s cute... but what''s with the tire?  If it''s to be played with... then... what''s with the door?  The subjects compete with each other, in my opinion.  I just don''t understand.     (not voting) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Guess when you are from a context things seem natural together. Little boys in Africa play with tires, this little guy lives in old town Zanzibar and was standing in front of the door of his house. He sat for at least 15 minutes playing with this old tire, perhaps his only toy. When I look at the picture I see a boy at his house watching people go by, looking for a friend to play with him.</td>', 'Originally posted by LydiaToo: Nope.... I don''t understand similar entry either... She''s cute... but what''s with the tire?  If it''s to be played with... then... what''s with the door?  The subjects compete with each other, in my opinion.  I just don''t understand.     (not voting)   Guess when you are from a context things seem natural together. Little boys in Africa play with tires, this little guy lives in old town Zanzibar and was standing in front of the door of his house. He sat for at least 15 minutes playing with this old tire, perhaps his only toy. When I look at the picture I see a boy at his house watching people go by, looking for a friend to play with him.', '2011-06-08 14:03:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(6438650, 954543, 30214, '<td valign="top">nice peaceful street scene, great BW. Congrats on top 5, John!</td>', 'nice peaceful street scene, great BW. Congrats on top 5, John!', '2011-06-08 14:36:09.000000', NULL, 0),
