(6439823, 952806, 2158, '<td valign="top">You have picked very difficult lighting for this shot.  For the scene to look good you really need to work with HDR software and bracketed images at different exposures.  Unfortunately good photos are often as much dependent on post-processing as on what comes out of the camera.  If the sun hadn''t been in the picture you wouldn''t have had all that glare and this would have come out much better.<br/> <br/>Don''t be discouraged by the way this looks.  You''re at the beginning of a great adventure and you will learn from your mistakes.</td>', 'You have picked very difficult lighting for this shot.  For the scene to look good you really need to work with HDR software and bracketed images at different exposures.  Unfortunately good photos are often as much dependent on post-processing as on what comes out of the camera.  If the sun hadn''t been in the picture you wouldn''t have had all that glare and this would have come out much better. Don''t be discouraged by the way this looks.  You''re at the beginning of a great adventure and you will learn from your mistakes.', '2011-06-09 21:40:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(6439890, 951393, 54645, '<td valign="top">Great capture Lev. A reminder of what we don''t usually see.</td>', 'Great capture Lev. A reminder of what we don''t usually see.', '2011-06-10 00:17:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(6440267, 953692, 108580, '<td valign="top">Perhaps the Church need a few hidden strobes to kick it up a notch, but for me I enjoyed it as it is. 8.</td>', 'Perhaps the Church need a few hidden strobes to kick it up a notch, but for me I enjoyed it as it is. 8.', '2011-06-10 07:17:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(6440336, 953408, 108580, '<td valign="top">You have a superb camera with 51 focus points, but they get in the way of Macro/Close-Up photography. Switch OFF APS-C or APS-S and use manual focus or use selective focus points and tell the camera where YOU want it to focus (p78 in the D300s manual) Increase you aperture to f/8 at least for this kind of shot. f/4.4 is not enough. What lens did you use?</td>', 'You have a superb camera with 51 focus points, but they get in the way of Macro/Close-Up photography. Switch OFF APS-C or APS-S and use manual focus or use selective focus points and tell the camera where YOU want it to focus (p78 in the D300s manual) Increase you aperture to f/8 at least for this kind of shot. f/4.4 is not enough. What lens did you use?', '2011-06-10 09:13:57.000000', NULL, 0),
