(6441647, 954339, 124815, '<td valign="top">Just realized that I am never surprised where my images get in the final counting of marks, but I am truly stunned by the lack of response to this spectacular image during the voting. It''s as close to what one could call a "flawless" image from a lot of points of view.  <br/>The discrepancy between the average marks given by commentators and participants is staggering. <br/>Perhaps the true mark of a great image (piece of art) is not being recognized as such immediately. <br/>Does the majority appreciate mostly the familiar, the nonthreatening, the technically solid work? A question as old as the world. <br/>I had 5 images on my first page and none was among the 10 most admired pictures.</td>', 'Just realized that I am never surprised where my images get in the final counting of marks, but I am truly stunned by the lack of response to this spectacular image during the voting. It''s as close to what one could call a "flawless" image from a lot of points of view.  The discrepancy between the average marks given by commentators and participants is staggering. Perhaps the true mark of a great image (piece of art) is not being recognized as such immediately. Does the majority appreciate mostly the familiar, the nonthreatening, the technically solid work? A question as old as the world. I had 5 images on my first page and none was among the 10 most admired pictures.', '2011-06-12 01:48:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(6441691, 954818, 54645, '<td valign="top">Beautiful portrait.</td>', 'Beautiful portrait.', '2011-06-12 05:05:28.000000', NULL, 0),
